---
/**
 * about.astro
 * Technical architecture, hardware specifications, and project overview for Call of the Wintermon.
 */

import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Technical Architecture & Hardware Specs — Call of the Wintermon"
  description="Comprehensive technical analysis of the Atari 800XL / 65XE hardware, MOS 6502 engine, ANTIC, GTIA, and POKEY."
>
  <div class="space-y-10">

    <!-- Page Header -->
    <div class="border-b border-atari-border pb-6 space-y-2">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-atari-green font-bold tracking-wider uppercase">
        <span>&gt; DOCUMENTATION</span>
        <span class="text-atari-muted">/</span>
        <span>ATARI 8-BIT XL/XE HARDWARE ARCHITECTURE</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-atari-text font-mono">
        ENGINEERING &amp; <span class="text-atari-green">HARDWARE ARCHITECTURE</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-atari-muted leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        Call of the Wintermon is built from the ground up to demonstrate modern software engineering practices
        applied to historical 8-bit embedded constraints: 100% MOS 6502 assembly language, deterministic frame scheduling,
        hardware register pipelining, and automated Python asset compilers.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 1. The Custom Chips (The Atari Trinity) -->
    <section class="space-y-4 font-mono">
      <div class="border-b border-atari-border pb-3">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-atari-text uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-atari-green">&gt;</span>
          <span>THE ATARI CUSTOM CO-PROCESSORS</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-atari-muted mt-0.5">
          Dedicated silicon co-processors designed by Jay Miner that defined the Atari 8-bit architecture.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        
        <!-- ANTIC -->
        <div class="border border-atari-border bg-atari-surface/70 rounded-lg p-5 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-atari-border/50 pb-2">
            <span class="font-bold text-atari-green text-sm">ANTIC (Alpha-Numeric TV Interface Controller)</span>
            <span class="text-[11px] text-atari-cyan font-mono">$D400 - $D4FF</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-atari-muted leading-relaxed">
            A true graphics microprocessor running its own instruction set concurrently with the 6502. 
            ANTIC fetches Display Lists via direct memory access (DMA), controlling screen geometry on a line-by-line basis.
          </p>
          <ul class="text-xs text-atari-muted/90 space-y-1 list-disc list-inside">
            <li><strong class="text-atari-text">Display Lists:</strong> Dynamic instruction pipelines driving ANTIC Mode E (160×96 2bpp).</li>
            <li><strong class="text-atari-text">DLI Support:</strong> Bit 7 interrupts halting the 6502 to reload GTIA color palettes on the fly.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-atari-text">Fine Scrolling:</strong> Hardware horizontal and vertical pixel fine-scroll registers (<code class="text-atari-green">HSCROL</code>, <code class="text-atari-green">VSCROL</code>).</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- GTIA -->
        <div class="border border-atari-border bg-atari-surface/70 rounded-lg p-5 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-atari-border/50 pb-2">
            <span class="font-bold text-atari-cyan text-sm">GTIA (Graphic Television Interface Adapter)</span>
            <span class="text-[11px] text-atari-cyan font-mono">$D000 - $D01F</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-atari-muted leading-relaxed">
            Converts ANTIC digital video signals into analog composite video (lum/chroma).
            Manages the 128/256-color palette, Player-Missile Graphics, and hardware collision detection registers.
          </p>
          <ul class="text-xs text-atari-muted/90 space-y-1 list-disc list-inside">
            <li><strong class="text-atari-text">Player-Missile Graphics:</strong> 4 hardware players and 4 missiles with independent horizontal positions (<code class="text-atari-cyan">HPOSP0-HPOSP3</code>).</li>
            <li><strong class="text-atari-text">Hardware Collisions:</strong> Instant silicon collision latches (<code class="text-atari-cyan">M0PF</code>, <code class="text-atari-cyan">P0PF</code>, <code class="text-atari-cyan">M0PL</code>).</li>
            <li><strong class="text-atari-text">Console Keys:</strong> Direct read of START, SELECT, and OPTION buttons (<code class="text-atari-cyan">CONSOL</code>).</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- POKEY -->
        <div class="border border-atari-border bg-atari-surface/70 rounded-lg p-5 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-atari-border/50 pb-2">
            <span class="font-bold text-atari-amber text-sm">POKEY (Potentiometers &amp; Keyboard)</span>
            <span class="text-[11px] text-atari-cyan font-mono">$D200 - $D2FF</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-atari-muted leading-relaxed">
            The multi-function audio/input chip. Provides 4 independent polyphonic audio channels, 
            random noise generators, high-speed serial I/O, timers, and matrix keyboard scanning.
          </p>
          <ul class="text-xs text-atari-muted/90 space-y-1 list-disc list-inside">
            <li><strong class="text-atari-text">4 Audio Channels:</strong> Frequency dividers (<code class="text-atari-amber">AUDF1-4</code>) and distortion control (<code class="text-atari-amber">AUDC1-4</code>).</li>
            <li><strong class="text-atari-text">Timers &amp; Polynomials:</strong> 4-bit, 5-bit, 9-bit, and 17-bit polynomial noise generation.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-atari-text">Sound Engine:</strong> Custom 50 Hz VBLANK driver executing music scores and priority SFX.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- MOS 6502 & PIA 6520 -->
        <div class="border border-atari-border bg-atari-surface/70 rounded-lg p-5 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-atari-border/50 pb-2">
            <span class="font-bold text-atari-text text-sm">MOS 6502 CPU &amp; PIA 6520</span>
            <span class="text-[11px] text-atari-cyan font-mono">1.77 MHz (PAL) / $D300</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-atari-muted leading-relaxed">
            The central 8-bit processing unit running at 1.773447 MHz on PAL systems.
            Communicates with joystick ports and system memory banking via the 6520 PIA.
          </p>
          <ul class="text-xs text-atari-muted/90 space-y-1 list-disc list-inside">
            <li><strong class="text-atari-text">PORTB ($D301):</strong> Memory banking register controlling BASIC ROM and OS ROM visibility.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-atari-text">Deterministic Timing:</strong> Strict instruction cycle budgets per scanline (114 system cycles per scanline).</li>
            <li><strong class="text-atari-text">Zero Page ($80-$FF):</strong> Fast 1-cycle-saving addressable scratchpad registers for game physics and rendering pointers.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 2. Deterministic Frame Pipeline -->
    <section class="border border-atari-border bg-atari-surface/60 rounded-lg p-5 space-y-4 font-mono text-xs">
      <div class="border-b border-atari-border pb-3">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-atari-text uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-atari-green">&gt;</span>
          <span>DETERMINISTIC 50 HZ FRAME PIPELINE</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-atari-muted mt-0.5">
          Fixed phase execution scheduled once per PAL frame (every 20 ms).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-6 gap-3">
        <div class="border border-atari-border/40 bg-atari-surfaceLight/30 rounded p-3 space-y-1">
          <div class="font-bold text-atari-cyan text-[11px]">1. INPUT POLL</div>
          <p class="text-[10px] text-atari-muted leading-relaxed">
            Sample PIA <code class="text-atari-text">PORTA</code> joystick directions and <code class="text-atari-text">TRIG0</code> fire button with debouncing.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-atari-border/40 bg-atari-surfaceLight/30 rounded p-3 space-y-1">
          <div class="font-bold text-atari-green text-[11px]">2. ENTITY UPDATE</div>
          <p class="text-[10px] text-atari-muted leading-relaxed">
            Update player velocity, moving platforms, patrol enemies, and animation frame counters.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-atari-border/40 bg-atari-surfaceLight/30 rounded p-3 space-y-1">
          <div class="font-bold text-atari-amber text-[11px]">3. COLLISION</div>
          <p class="text-[10px] text-atari-muted leading-relaxed">
            Evaluate bounding box intersections against platform tiles, enemy hitboxes, and collectible secrets.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-atari-border/40 bg-atari-surfaceLight/30 rounded p-3 space-y-1">
          <div class="font-bold text-atari-text text-[11px]">4. STATE UPDATE</div>
          <p class="text-[10px] text-atari-muted leading-relaxed">
            Transition game states (Playing, Game Over, Stage Victory) and update life and score counters.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-atari-border/40 bg-atari-surfaceLight/30 rounded p-3 space-y-1">
          <div class="font-bold text-purple-400 text-[11px]">5. PREPARE BUFFERS</div>
          <p class="text-[10px] text-atari-muted leading-relaxed">
            Write PMG player/missile slices into active RAM buffers and build DLI scanline tables.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-atari-border/40 bg-atari-surfaceLight/30 rounded p-3 space-y-1">
          <div class="font-bold text-red-400 text-[11px]">6. SWAP &amp; VBLANK</div>
          <p class="text-[10px] text-atari-muted leading-relaxed">
            VBLANK NMI commits display list pointers, ticks POKEY music driver, and resets color shadows.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. Toolchain & Development Methodology -->
    <section class="border border-atari-border bg-atari-surface/60 rounded-lg p-5 space-y-4 font-mono text-xs">
      <div class="border-b border-atari-border pb-3">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-atari-text uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-atari-cyan">&gt;</span>
          <span>MODERN TOOLING FOR VINTAGE SILICON</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-atari-muted mt-0.5">
          Integrating modern Python build pipelines with native 6502 cross-assembly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-atari-green text-xs">MADS (Mad Assembler 2.1.6)</h3>
          <p class="text-atari-muted leading-relaxed text-[11px]">
            Fast 6502/65C02 macro cross-assembler. Compiles modular assembly files into single-pass XEX binaries
            with automatic label export (<code class="text-atari-text">main.lab</code>) and listing maps (<code class="text-atari-text">main.lst</code>).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-atari-cyan text-xs">PYTHON SSOT DATA COMPILERS</h3>
          <p class="text-atari-muted leading-relaxed text-[11px]">
            YAML and JSON source-of-truth files (<code class="text-atari-text">manifest.yaml</code>, <code class="text-atari-text">scenes.json</code>)
            are parsed via Pydantic and compiled directly into Structure-of-Arrays (SoA) assembly tables, 
            guaranteeing zero runtime overhead for the 6502.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-atari-amber text-xs">AUTOMATED PY65 &amp; MEMORY VERIFICATION</h3>
          <p class="text-atari-muted leading-relaxed text-[11px]">
            Continuous verification via <code class="text-atari-text">py65</code> CPU emulation harnesses.
            Automated scripts (<code class="text-atari-text">check_memory.py</code>, <code class="text-atari-text">generate_memory_map.py</code>)
            enforce segment bounds and verify headroom below $C000 before any binary is released.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-atari-green text-xs">DUAL-LANGUAGE LOCALIZATION (EN &amp; PL)</h3>
          <p class="text-atari-muted leading-relaxed text-[11px]">
            Call of the Wintermon releases feature native English (<code class="text-atari-text">call_of_the_wintermon_en.xex</code>)
            and Polish (<code class="text-atari-text">call_of_the_wintermon_pl.xex</code>) binaries compiled via conditional
            MADS assembly (<code class="text-atari-text">-d:LANG_EN=1</code>). Both versions share a unified 1 KB Atari character set
            mapped to full Latin and Polish diacritics with zero runtime RAM overhead.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 4. Project Repository Links & Credits -->
    <section class="border border-atari-border bg-atari-surface/60 rounded-lg p-5 space-y-4 font-mono text-xs">
      <div class="border-b border-atari-border pb-3">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-atari-text uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-atari-green">&gt;</span>
          <span>PROJECT REPOSITORY &amp; CREDITS</span>
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <div>
          <div class="text-sm font-bold text-atari-text">CALL OF THE WINTERMON</div>
          <div class="text-xs text-atari-muted">An open-source Atari 8-bit platform adventure game.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <a
            href="https://github.com/grzes71/call-of-the-wintermon"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="px-4 py-2 rounded bg-atari-green text-atari-dark font-bold text-xs uppercase hover:bg-atari-greenDim transition-colors shadow-atari-green"
          >
            VIEW GITHUB REPO
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/grzes71/call-of-the-wintermon/issues"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="px-4 py-2 rounded border border-atari-border text-atari-muted hover:text-atari-text text-xs uppercase"
          >
            REPORT AN ISSUE
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>

